WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.758
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:15.600
Unit nine: Future Continuous. Today you will describe actions in progress at a future moment.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.552
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.733
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.480
Will be.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.017
Will be means the future continuous helper.

8
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:29.850
I will be working.

9
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.766
Your turn. Say: Will be.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.717
Will be.

11
00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:38.310
-ing.

12
00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:40.991
-ing means the verb ending.

13
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:42.910
Working, travelling.

14
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:45.438
Your turn. Say: -ing.

15
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:48.930
-ing.

16
00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:51.288
Ongoing future action.

17
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:55.711
Ongoing future action means an action in progress later.

18
00:00:56.317 --> 00:00:58.061
An ongoing future action.

19
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.929
Your turn. Say: Ongoing future action.

20
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.650
Ongoing future action.

21
00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.987
At a specific time.

22
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.900
At a specific time means at an exact moment.

23
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:14.785
At six o'clock.

24
00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:18.547
Your turn. Say: At a specific time.

25
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.040
At a specific time.

26
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:24.680
Prediction.

27
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:27.764
Prediction means a guess about the future.

28
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.827
A confident prediction.

29
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:32.848
Your turn. Say: Prediction.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.399
Prediction.

31
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.430
In progress.

32
00:01:39.417 --> 00:01:42.194
In progress means happening and not finished.

33
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:44.272
The work is in progress.

34
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.431
Your turn. Say: In progress.

35
00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.500
In progress.

36
00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.274
Future moment.

37
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:56.643
Future moment means a point in the future.

38
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.518
A future moment.

39
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:01.583
Your turn. Say: Future moment.

40
00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:05.620
Future moment.

41
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:07.837
This time tomorrow.

42
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.349
This time tomorrow means at the same hour tomorrow.

43
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.950
This time tomorrow I'll be flying.

44
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.458
Your turn. Say: This time tomorrow.

45
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.858
This time tomorrow.

46
00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:26.062
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:29.706
Visal, what will you be doing this time tomorrow?

48
00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:42.281
This time tomorrow I will be flying to Phnom Penh. The future continuous, will be plus the -ing form, shows an action in progress at a particular future moment.

49
00:02:43.383 --> 00:02:44.965
What other uses are there?

50
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:57.712
Polite questions about plans: Will you be using the car tonight? And predictions about what is happening now: Don't call him; he'll be sleeping.

51
00:02:58.817 --> 00:03:00.921
How is it different from the future perfect?

52
00:03:02.017 --> 00:03:17.222
Future continuous is in progress at a time: At nine I will be teaching. Future perfect is finished before a time: By nine I will have taught. State verbs like know or want do not take the continuous.

53
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.925
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:24.966
Grammar focus: Future continuous: will be plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:25.266 --> 00:03:26.522
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:27.217 --> 00:03:29.762
This time tomorrow I will be flying to Phnom Penh.

57
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.870
At nine she will be teaching a class.

58
00:03:33.783 --> 00:03:35.748
Will you be using the car tonight?

59
00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:45.866
Will be + verb-ing = in progress at a future moment, or a polite question about plans. Compare: future perfect = finished before that moment.

60
00:03:46.617 --> 00:03:50.186
Be careful! Don't say: At nine I will teach a class.

61
00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.189
Say: At nine I will be teaching a class.

62
00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:57.373
Use the future continuous.

63
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.564
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.786
In Progress Later.

65
00:04:03.086 --> 00:04:05.735
This time tomorrow I will be flying to Phnom Penh.

66
00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:10.231
At nine o'clock my sister will be teaching her first class.

67
00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:14.002
Will you be using the car tonight? I need it.

68
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.371
Don't call him now; he will be sleeping.

69
00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:21.272
These are predictions about moments that are in progress.

70
00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:26.496
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.210
At noon I blank in a meeting.

72
00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:33.257
A, sit. B, will be sitting. C, will have sat.

73
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.020
The answer is B: will be sitting.

74
00:04:40.183 --> 00:04:42.740
This time next year, she blank in Paris.

75
00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.228
A, will be studying. B, will have studied. C, studies.

76
00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:53.335
The answer is A: will be studying.

77
00:04:54.483 --> 00:04:56.088
Which is a polite question?

78
00:04:56.388 --> 00:05:02.189
A, Give me the car.. B, Are you using the car or not?. C, Will you be using the car?.

79
00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:08.453
The answer is C: Will you be using the car?.

80
00:05:09.617 --> 00:05:12.069
Which verb cannot take the continuous?

81
00:05:12.369 --> 00:05:15.198
A, know. B, run. C, work.

82
00:05:18.733 --> 00:05:20.431
The answer is A: know.

83
00:05:21.583 --> 00:05:24.407
According to the reading, what will the sister be doing?

84
00:05:24.707 --> 00:05:28.012
A, teaching. B, flying. C, sleeping.

85
00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.439
The answer is A: teaching.

86
00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:37.797
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.694
Write a sentence about what you will be doing this time next week.

88
00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.088
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:52.388 --> 00:06:06.107
This time tomorrow I will be sitting in a lecture hall, taking notes about economics. At lunchtime I will be meeting my friends. I use the future continuous for actions in progress at a future moment.

90
00:06:06.407 --> 00:06:08.175
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:14.534
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future continuous: will be plus verb-ing.

92
00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:19.680
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.319
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:06:22.619 --> 00:06:25.353
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

